      "prompt": "Save the brief between the markers as <brief-file>, then run (one line, the brief read from the file):\ncodex exec --json -o <last-message-file> --output-schema <schema-file> --worktree -C <dir> \"$(cat <brief-file>)\"\n--- brief ---\npython3 docs/ai-forward-pack/scripts/audit-log.py start --session cfd-coordinator-20260923 --skill prepare-for-coordination\nGoal state\nGoal: Update the pack and deliver verified, coordinated application increments from the authoritative CFD-Workbench and FoilDSL contracts.\nDone when: The latest pack and coordination layer are verified.; A concrete first milestone, architecture, ownership plan, and model routing table are recorded.; Qualified harness sessions implement and integrate dependency-ready increments with runnable results and reviewed proof.\nNot in scope: Public deployment, purchases, unrelated credentials, destructive operations outside task scope, and trust or platform bypass.; Prototype calculations or illustrative scientific results presented as production claims.\nTier: T2\nFan-out cap: 3\nContext ceiling: 100000\nMain-line budget: Initial 70 tool calls / 30 minutes for qualification and plan; replan on cap without dropping gates.\nTrace\n| clause | trace |\n|---|---|\n| done_when: The latest pack and coordination layer are verified. | phrase: Verify the update using its required checks. |\n| done_when: A concrete first milestone, architecture, ownership plan, and model routing table are recorded. | phrase: Set a concrete first delivery milestone, its acceptance criteria, non-goals, and proof obligations. |\n| done_when: Qualified harness sessions implement and integrate dependency-ready increments with runnable results and reviewed proof. | phrase: This Codex session must launch and manage the other harness sessions through the repository’s supported coordination mechanisms. |\n| not_in_scope: Public deployment, purchases, unrelated credentials, destructive operations outside task scope, and trust or platform bypass. | phrase: It does not authorize overriding platform restrictions, accessing unrelated credentials, destructive operations outside task scope, purchasing services, or deploying publicly. |\n| not_in_scope: Prototype calculations or illustrative scientific results presented as production claims. | phrase: Prototype calculations and illustrative scientific results must not become production claims. |\nReferences\n- AGENTS.md: AGENTS.md sha256 af6d8f9e4823fb6d2af28ab38f6b302e0b8d3daf5d9078adfcc551135b3d04ae\n- docs/ai-forward-pack/codex.md: docs/ai-forward-pack/codex.md sha256 ca71039709e5bb87782f5bf2474f8a4018ccef4b066d353a9e3965d537f4d153\n- Claude/Fable: unresolved (not found)\n- Codex/Astra: unresolved (not found)\n- unattended/full-auto: unresolved (not found)\n- Windows/macOS: unresolved (not found)\n- leading/trailing: unresolved (not found)\n- harness/model: unresolved (not found)\nAssumptions\n- none\nDecision requests\n- none\nContract slot\nwidth_cap: 2\ntransient_retry: One pre-dispatch retry for a clean startup failure; no post-dispatch replay.\nper_branch_exit: Committed owned artifact and named proof are returned.\njoin_rule: All milestone-critical tracks must pass independent review and integrated gates; partial work remains unmerged and reported.\ncontainment: A failed branch stops only that branch; Owner rules any reassignment.\ntermination: Every dependency-ready track has verified exit evidence or a recorded blocker and fallback.\ndeadline: Per-track bounds in coordination plan.\nfallback: Retain brief and re-route through a qualified harness after Owner review.\nRules: absolute paths only; a multi-line program is a file, then a run; a gate's exit status is never behind a pipe.\nProvenance\nraw id: al-01M376G6MEVMMTPKPYP4GGBGVD\nraw sha256: 40085a72ac89eaefc8e7ad2139a3de0e326aa99da3db3dff1c85abf1c80ab4f3\ncompiler model: gpt-6-sol\nengine seconds: 0.001\ntokens: not recorded\ngate: pass\ndispatchable: true\n--- end brief ---\n",
