      "prompt": "Goal: Add Insert CV and Delete CV constructions for profile sections in the CFD-Workbench core, per docs/design/section-editor.md §9 row B1, under TDD.\nDone when: BeginProfileInsert and BeginProfileDelete exist with the §9 contract; insert preserves shape to 1e-12 relative on both sides and keeps the paired abscissa; delete reports the maximum shape change and refuses below p + 2 = 7 vertices with a reason; Preview/Apply/Cancel/Undo/Redo work as for vertex moves (one undo item); tests/CfdWorkbench.Core.Tests/ConstructionTests.cs holds the listed checks and is registered in IdentityTests.cs Main; tools/run-tests.sh ends with \"all test harnesses passed\"; python3 tools/check-docs.py exits 0; committed on feature/section-insert-delete.\nNot in scope: Fair, Rebuild, Fit points, ConstrainedFit.cs (another track); Geometry.cs; Desktop; docs; changing existing public signatures; pushing; touching main or other worktrees.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 400000\nMain-line budget: 120 tool calls, 60 minutes\n\n## Harness notes (Grok Build)\n- Working directory: /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-insert-delete (branch feature/section-insert-delete). Stay inside it. No worktrees, no push.\n- AGENTS.md is loaded. Follow the `/implement` loop (.grok/skills/implement/SKILL.md): red → green → refactor. No persona sub-agents, no rulings, ledgers, proof packets or audit entries.\n- Repair loops are capped at 2 cycles. Same failure twice → stop and report.\n\n## Read first (only these)\n1. docs/design/section-editor.md §2 (Shared abscissa), §4.1, §9 (B1 row).\n2. src/CfdWorkbench.Core/AuthoringSession.cs — BeginProfileEdit/UpdateProfileDraft and how a draft's bytes, generation and receipt are built; Validate/Apply.\n3. src/CfdWorkbench.Core/FoilSource.cs — PatchProfilePoint and how a curve's knots/points/ids tokens are located and rewritten (exact shortest decimals).\n4. src/CfdWorkbench.Core/Geometry.cs — read-only: how profile sides are evaluated (to measure shape preservation), the degree-5 / N∈[6,32] rules.\n\n## Contract\n- `SessionDraft BeginProfileInsert(string draftId, int assignmentIndex, SectionScope scope, double x)` — inserts one knot at the curve parameter where the side's x(t) = x, on BOTH sides (the sides share knots and CV x, so the same parameter applies), via Boehm knot insertion; new vertex ids follow the existing id scheme and never reuse a deleted id. Refuse x outside (0,1) or N = 32 with DSL-PROFILE-TARGET / DSL-CURVE.\n- `SessionDraft BeginProfileDelete(string draftId, int assignmentIndex, SectionScope scope, int vertexIndex)` — removes the paired vertex on both sides by knot removal (least-squares removal is acceptable); first and last vertex are Fixed → DSL-LOCK; below 7 vertices → DSL-CURVE with reason \"Delete would leave fewer than p + 2 = 7 vertices\".\n- Add `public sealed record ConstructionReport(double MaxDeviation, double? Tolerance, int VertexCount);` to the end of Contracts.cs and expose it on SessionAssessment as an optional `ConstructionReport? Construction` property (default null so existing callers are unaffected). MaxDeviation is the maximum |Δy| between old and new side curves over 2001 samples in x, both sides.\n- Scope works as for vertex edits (Independent makes the copy first).\n\n## Tests — ConstructionTests.Run(), registered in IdentityTests.cs Main (red first)\n- Insert at x = 0.37 on the Example: both sides gain one vertex, knots match across sides, MaxDeviation ≤ 1e-12 relative to chord, Validate Certified, Apply → Undo restores exact bytes, Redo restores the insert.\n- Insert then Delete of the inserted vertex: shape returns to the original within 1e-12.\n- Delete an interior original vertex: MaxDeviation reported (> 0), Validate Certified or a named geometry refusal — never an unreported change.\n- Delete when N = 7 → DSL-CURVE with the reason text; delete first vertex → DSL-LOCK.\n- Cancel after Insert restores exact bytes; one Undo item per construction.\n\n## Verify, then commit\n- `tools/run-tests.sh` → `all test harnesses passed`. `python3 tools/check-docs.py` → exit 0 (own line).\n- Commit: `feat: insert and delete paired profile control vertices`, trailer `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>`.\n\n## Return (final message only)\nCommit SHA; files changed; new public members; PASS lines; last lines of run-tests.sh and check-docs; anything not done and why.",
