          "main_line_budget": "120 tool calls, 60 minutes\n## Harness notes (Grok Build)\nWorking directory: /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-fit-fair (branch feature/section-fit-fair). Stay inside it. No worktrees, no push.\nAGENTS.md is loaded. Follow the `/implement` loop (.grok/skills/implement/SKILL.md): red → green → refactor. No persona sub-agents, no rulings, ledgers, proof packets or audit entries.\nRepair loops are capped at 2 cycles. Same failure twice → stop and report.\n## Read first (only these)\n1. docs/specs/cfd-workbench-v1.md L395-420 (Fit points, Fair, Rebuild, constraint catalogue) and the GEO-15 row (search \"GEO-15\").\n2. docs/design/section-editor.md §2 (Shared abscissa) and §9.\n3. src/CfdWorkbench.Core/FoilSource.cs — the Curve and ProfileDefinition records only (degree, knots, points).\n4. src/CfdWorkbench.Core/Geometry.cs — read-only: how a profile side is evaluated (Cox–de Boor / Bernstein), to reuse for sampling Q and measuring deviation.\n## Design (implement exactly; ask nothing — report if impossible)\n`ConstrainedFit.Solve(double[,] N, double[] q, double[] w, double[,] F, double lambda, double[,] A, double[] b) -> double[] p` : solve the KKT system [[NᵀWN + λF, Aᵀ],[A, 0]] [p; μ] = [NᵀWq; b] with a numerically stable dense solver (LU with partial pivoting is acceptable at these sizes, n ≤ 32). Refuse a singular system with ContractError(\"GEOMETRY-FIT-SINGULAR\").\nFairness functional F = ∫ (y''(x))² dx over the side, integrated exactly or with Gauss–Legendre per knot span (≥ p+1 points).\n**Fair(profile, tolerance, PreserveEnds ends)**: for each side, keep knots and CV x fixed; unknowns are the CV y; Q = the current side sampled at 201 Greville-spaced x; W = identity; A·P = b pins: first CV y = 0 always (LE); `position` pins last CV y; `tangency` also pins the second and second-to-last CV y; `curvature` also pins the third and third-to-last. Choose λ by bisection on log λ so the achieved max deviation is the largest ≤ tolerance (stop after 40 steps). Report `FairResult(Curve Upper, Curve Lower, double MaxDeviation, bool WithinTolerance, int MonotonePiecesBefore, int MonotonePiecesAfter)`. Accept only when WithinTolerance and MonotonePiecesAfter ≤ MonotonePiecesBefore (count sign changes of y' over 2001 samples, per side).\n**Rebuild(profile, int vertexCount, tolerance, ends)**: new clamped uniform knot vector for degree 5 with vertexCount CVs; the new CV x distribution is the Greville abscissae mapped through the old side's x(t) so both sides share it; fit y to Q by least squares with the same pins and the fairness term; same report and acceptance.\nBoth sides must end with identical knots and CV x (paired abscissa).\n## Tests — FitTests.Run(), registered in IdentityTests.cs Main (red first)\nSolve reproduces an exact polynomial fit (Q sampled from a known degree-5 curve on the same knots; λ = 0) to 1e-12.\nSolve honours equality constraints exactly (A·p − b ≤ 1e-12) and refuses a singular system.\nFair on the Example profile with tolerance 1e-4: MaxDeviation ≤ 1e-4, fairness functional decreases or stays equal, LE y = 0, monotone pieces not increased, knots and x unchanged on both sides.\nFair with a tolerance of 1e-15 → WithinTolerance false (nothing to accept without changing shape), or MaxDeviation = 0 with unchanged curves.\nRebuild to 10 CVs: both sides have 10 CVs, identical knots and x, MaxDeviation reported, pins honoured.\nPreserveEnds `tangency` keeps the second and second-to-last CV y unchanged.\n## Verify, then commit\n`tools/run-tests.sh` → `all test harnesses passed`. `python3 tools/check-docs.py` → exit 0 (own line).\nCommit: `feat: add the constrained fit solver with profile fair and rebuild`, trailer `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>`.\n## Return (final message only)\nCommit SHA; files changed; public members of ConstrainedFit and ProfileFair; PASS lines; last lines of run-tests.sh and check-docs; anything not done and why.",
