      "prompt": "Goal: Add the \"Use source thickness\" intent to CFD-Workbench section edits — an explicit, constrained edit of the foil-wide t/c channel — per docs/design/section-editor.md §9 row B3 and Product A4.14, under TDD.\nDone when: BeginProfileEdit accepts a ThicknessIntent (default KeepCurrent, so existing callers and tests are unchanged); with UseSource the draft also refits the `thickness` channel so t/c at each affected assignment equals the edited profile's max(upper − lower), using ConstrainedFit; the assessment carries a ThicknessProposal with targets, residuals and the affected η span; Apply is refused when the fit is infeasible or a residual exceeds 1e-9 absolute; the chosen intent is recorded on the edit receipt; tests/CfdWorkbench.Core.Tests/ThicknessIntentTests.cs holds the listed checks and is registered; tools/run-tests.sh ends with \"all test harnesses passed\"; python3 tools/check-docs.py exits 0; committed on feature/section-thickness.\nNot in scope: Geometry.cs; ConstrainedFit.cs internals (call its public Solve; report defects instead of editing it); Desktop; DAT import; any station-level t/c field (there must be none — derive, don't store); pushing; touching main or other worktrees.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 400000\nMain-line budget: 100 tool calls, 50 minutes\n\n## Harness notes (Grok Build)\n- Working directory: /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-thickness (branch feature/section-thickness). Stay inside it. No worktrees, no push.\n- AGENTS.md is loaded. Follow the `/implement` loop (.grok/skills/implement/SKILL.md): red → green → refactor. No persona sub-agents, rulings, ledgers, proof packets or audit entries.\n- Repair loops are capped at 2 cycles. Same failure twice → stop and report.\n\n## Read first (only these)\n1. docs/specs/cfd-workbench-v1.md A4.14 \"Thickness intent\" paragraph (search \"Thickness intent\") and docs/specs/foildsl.md §5 item 6 (thickness channel; \"Use source thickness\" is a one-transaction command).\n2. docs/design/section-editor.md §3, §9.\n3. src/CfdWorkbench.Core/ConstrainedFit.cs public surface; src/CfdWorkbench.Core/AuthoringSession.cs BeginProfileEdit/UpdateProfileDraft/ValidateCore and the edit receipt; src/CfdWorkbench.Core/FoilSource.cs PatchRail (the thickness channel is a planform channel patched like a rail).\n\n## Contract\n- In Contracts.cs (append): `public enum ThicknessIntent { KeepCurrent, UseSource }` and `public sealed record ThicknessProposal(IReadOnlyList<double> TargetEta, IReadOnlyList<double> TargetThickness, IReadOnlyList<double> Residuals, double AffectedEtaStart, double AffectedEtaEnd);` and an optional `ThicknessProposal? Thickness` on SessionAssessment (default null).\n- `BeginProfileEdit(..., ThicknessIntent thickness = ThicknessIntent.KeepCurrent)` — optional trailing parameter.\n- UseSource: after each UpdateProfileDraft, compute targets = max_x(upper − lower) of the edited profile at every affected assignment η (from DescribeScope); refit the thickness channel's CV ordinates (knots and CV abscissae fixed) with ConstrainedFit: Q = current channel sampled at 101 η, W = 1, λ small (1e-6), equality rows pinning the channel value at each target η, plus the channel's existing locks (root_mirror etc.) as rows; patch the thickness CVs in the draft source. AffectedEta = the η range where the channel changed by more than 1e-12. Infeasible or singular → the assessment is not Certified and names the reason (existing DSL-LOCK / GEOMETRY-FIT-SINGULAR codes).\n- KeepCurrent: identical to today (thickness channel bytes unchanged — assert it).\n\n## Tests — ThicknessIntentTests.Run(), registered in IdentityTests.cs Main (red first)\n- KeepCurrent: a profile edit leaves the thickness channel bytes identical (existing behaviour).\n- UseSource on the Example, shared scope: after thickening the upper side, t/c at root and tip equals the edited profile's max thickness within 1e-9; Residuals ≤ 1e-9; Apply → Undo restores profile and thickness bytes together; the receipt records UseSource.\n- UseSource on the 3-station independent case: only the middle target is imposed; AffectedEta is reported and lies within the channel's local support.\n- A lock that makes the target infeasible (e.g. a value lock at the target η with a different value) → not Certified, Apply refused, reason named.\n\n## Verify, then commit\n- `tools/run-tests.sh` → `all test harnesses passed`. `python3 tools/check-docs.py` → exit 0 (own line).\n- Commit: `feat: propose thickness-channel edits for use-source thickness intent`, trailer `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>`.\n\n## Return (final message only)\nCommit SHA; files changed; new public members; PASS lines; last lines of run-tests.sh and check-docs; anything not done and why.",
