      "outcome": "success",
      "prompt": "Goal: Expose Fair and Rebuild as session drafts in the CFD-Workbench core, reusing ProfileFair and the curve rewrite that Insert/Delete already use.\nDone when: AuthoringSession has BeginProfileFair and BeginProfileRebuild; each builds a draft whose profile curves are the ProfileFair result, carries a ConstructionReport (MaxDeviation, Tolerance, VertexCount) on the assessment, refuses Apply when the result is not WithinTolerance or the monotone-piece count increased, and behaves like Insert/Delete for Preview/Apply/Cancel/Undo/Redo (one undo item); the tests below pass and are registered; tools/run-tests.sh ends with \"all test harnesses passed\"; python3 tools/check-docs.py exits 0; one commit on feature/section-fair-session.\nNot in scope: ConstrainedFit.cs / ProfileFair internals (call them; report defects); Geometry.cs; Desktop; thickness intent; DAT import; pushing; touching main or other worktrees.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 400000\nMain-line budget: 60 tool calls\n\n## Where to work\nOnly in /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-fair-session (branch feature/section-fair-session). Absolute paths. No worktrees, no push. Repair loops capped at 2 — same failure twice, stop and report.\n\n## Facts (verified — do not re-investigate)\n- `ProfileFair.Fair(ProfileDefinition, double tolerance, PreserveEnds)` and `ProfileFair.Rebuild(ProfileDefinition, int vertexCount, double tolerance, PreserveEnds)` return `FairResult(Curve Upper, Curve Lower, double MaxDeviation, bool WithinTolerance, int MonotonePiecesBefore, int MonotonePiecesAfter)` (internal, src/CfdWorkbench.Core/ConstrainedFit.cs). `PreserveEnds` is Position | Tangency | Curvature.\n- Insert/Delete build drafts through `BeginProfileInsert` / `BeginProfileDelete` (src/CfdWorkbench.Core/AuthoringSession.cs ~L151-154) and rewrite both curves of a profile with `FoilSource.RewriteCurves(source, found, knots, upperPoints, upperIds, lowerPoints, lowerIds)` (src/CfdWorkbench.Core/FoilSource.cs, used at ~L299 and ~L324). `ConstructionReport(MaxDeviation, Tolerance?, VertexCount)` is in Contracts.cs and appears on SessionAssessment.\n- Scope works like Insert: Independent makes the copy first.\n\n## Build (red first) — mirror BeginProfileInsert exactly\n1. `public SessionDraft BeginProfileFair(string draftId, int assignmentIndex, SectionScope scope, double tolerance, PreserveEnds ends)` and `public SessionDraft BeginProfileRebuild(string draftId, int assignmentIndex, SectionScope scope, int vertexCount, double tolerance, PreserveEnds ends)`. PreserveEnds must be public for this signature: if it is internal, make the enum public (only that change in ConstrainedFit.cs). Rebuild keeps existing vertex ids where the count is unchanged, else issues fresh ids with the existing id scheme (never reuse a deleted id).\n2. The draft's assessment carries ConstructionReport(MaxDeviation, tolerance, VertexCount). When !WithinTolerance or MonotonePiecesAfter > MonotonePiecesBefore, Validate returns not-Certified with reason \"Fair result exceeds tolerance\" / \"Fair increased monotone pieces\" (code DSL-GEOMETRY) so Apply is refused.\n3. Tests — add `FairSessionTests.Run()` in tests/CfdWorkbench.Core.Tests/FairSessionTests.cs, registered in IdentityTests.cs Main: (a) Fair on the Example at tolerance 1e-4, Position → report MaxDeviation ≤ 1e-4, Validate Certified, Apply → Undo restores exact bytes, Redo re-applies; (b) Fair at tolerance 1e-15 → Apply refused, accepted bytes unchanged; (c) Rebuild to 10 vertices → both sides have 10 vertices, Certified, one undo item; (d) Cancel restores exact bytes.\n\n## Verify, then commit\n- `/Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-fair-session/tools/run-tests.sh` → `all test harnesses passed`.\n- `cd /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-fair-session && python3 tools/check-docs.py` → exit 0 (own line).\n- Commit: `feat: run profile fair and rebuild as session drafts`, trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n\n## Return (final message only)\nCommit SHA; files changed; PASS lines; last lines of run-tests.sh and check-docs; anything not done and why.",
