      "kind": "prompt",
      "outcome": "success",
      "prompt": "Goal: Make CFD-Workbench projects reopen after Insert, Delete, Fair or Rebuild — both accepted revisions and captured recovery drafts — by making the envelope reference check construction-aware (GEO-14, DSL-10).\nDone when: a project saved after an applied Insert, Delete, Fair or Rebuild reopens, and Undo/Redo still work after reopen; a project saved with a recovery captured mid-construction reopens and ResumeRecovery restores the draft; all existing envelope refusals still hold for rail and vertex edits; the tests below pass and are registered; tools/run-tests.sh ends with \"all test harnesses passed\"; python3 tools/check-docs.py exits 0; one commit on feature/section-reopen.\nNot in scope: the EditReceipt or RecoveryRow record shapes (no new fields); Geometry.cs; ConstrainedFit.cs; Desktop; thickness intent; DAT import; pushing; touching main or other worktrees.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 400000\nMain-line budget: 60 tool calls\n\n## Where to work\nOnly in /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-reopen (branch feature/section-reopen). Absolute paths. No worktrees, no push. Repair loops capped at 2 — same failure twice, stop and report.\n\n## Facts (verified — do not re-investigate)\n- Receipts: `EditReceipt(DraftId, Generation, Rail, VertexId)`. Construction drafts store the kind in Rail: \"insert\" (VertexId = the new vertex), \"delete\" (VertexId = the removed vertex), \"fair\" and \"rebuild\" (VertexId = the profile's first upper vertex id; Rebuild may issue new ids). See OpenConstruction calls in src/CfdWorkbench.Core/AuthoringSession.cs (~L391-424).\n- `static bool EditTarget(Definition, string channel, string vertexId)` (~L733) knows only leading/trailing/upper/lower and returns false otherwise.\n- Accepted-edit check (~L760 child, ~L762 parent) requires EditTarget on BOTH the child and the parent source.\n- Recovery check (~L772) allows only `r.Rail is \"leading\" or \"trailing\" or \"upper\" or \"lower\"` and then requires EditTarget on the base definition; a following block validates r.Profile / r.Assignment when Profile is non-null.\n\n## Rules to implement\nLet ProfileHas(d, id) = any profile's upper or lower Ids contains id.\n- Accepted edit, by Rail: leading/trailing/upper/lower → unchanged. insert → ProfileHas(child) required; parent not required. delete → ProfileHas(parent) required; child not required. fair → ProfileHas(child) and ProfileHas(parent). rebuild → ProfileHas(child) required; parent not required. Any other Rail → refuse (DOC-REFERENCE), as today.\n- Recovery, by Rail: allow insert/delete/fair/rebuild in addition to today's four; require r.Profile non-null for those four; vertex check against the base definition: delete and fair → ProfileHas(base); insert and rebuild → no vertex check against base (the r.Profile block still validates the profile and assignment against the recovered draft source).\nKeep the code as small as the surrounding style: one helper plus the per-kind switch.\n\n## Tests (red first) — add `ReopenConstructionTests.Run()` in tests/CfdWorkbench.Core.Tests/ReopenConstructionTests.cs, registered in IdentityTests.cs Main. Follow how existing tests save and reopen a session (grep `Reopen` / `ProjectStore` in tests/CfdWorkbench.Core.Tests).\n- For each of Insert (x = 0.37), Delete (an interior vertex), Fair (tolerance 1e-4, Position), Rebuild (10 vertices) on the Example: Apply, save, reopen → succeeds; the reopened accepted source bytes equal the pre-save bytes; Undo after reopen restores the pre-construction bytes; Redo restores the construction.\n- Capture recovery mid-Insert and mid-Rebuild, save, reopen → succeeds and ResumeRecovery yields a draft whose bytes equal the captured draft bytes.\n- A receipt with Rail \"bogus\" still refuses with DOC-REFERENCE (existing behaviour).\nStore tests need a real-path TMPDIR: always run through tools/run-tests.sh.\n\n## Verify, then commit\n- `/Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-reopen/tools/run-tests.sh` → `all test harnesses passed`.\n- `cd /Users/mallalieut/projects/CFD-Workbench-feature-section-reopen && python3 tools/check-docs.py` → exit 0 (own line).\n- Commit: `fix: reopen projects after profile constructions and their recovery drafts`, trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n\n## Return (final message only)\nCommit SHA; files changed; PASS lines; last lines of run-tests.sh and check-docs; anything not done and why.",
