      "prompt": "python3 docs/ai-forward-pack/scripts/audit-log.py start --session cfd-arch-author-20260923 --skill define-architecture\nGoal: Author the first CFD-Workbench application architecture, evidence-backed stack ruling proposal, and detailed first offline workbench slice design.\nDone when: The four assigned documents and three reproducible spike source files below are committed on your isolated branch; each contract gate has measured evidence or is explicitly Not assessed; the Owner has a typed decision request; the root can independently review the proof.\nNot in scope: Production application implementation, solver/analysis/export/AI features, editing normative specs or mockup, stack selection by prototype inheritance, claiming Windows live proof from macOS, altering pack/coordination files, using approval or trust bypass, spawning subagents.\nTier: T2\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 100000 tokens; at the ceiling compact or hand back the exact unfinished contract, never continue with a silent truncated context.\nMain-line budget: 70 tool calls and 50 minutes; a cap signals a planning defect and requires a report to the Coordinator, not a self-granted increase.\n\nSeat: Sub-Agent author. Coordinator cfd-coordinator-20260923; technical Owner/ruling seat cfd-owner-20260923. The Owner is not your co-author. Root is independent veto reviewer. Work only in the runner-assigned worktree; never invoke a host worktree-switching tool, create another worktree, install the coordination layer, edit another track, or spawn teams. Your exact authored path set is:\n- docs/architecture/application.md\n- docs/adr/0003-application-stack.md\n- docs/design/application-foundation.md\n- docs/proof/application-spikes.md\n- tools/spikes/ApplicationNativeUi/ApplicationNativeUi.csproj\n- tools/spikes/ApplicationNativeUi/Program.cs\n- tools/spikes/application-contract-vectors.py\nUse an untracked disposable scratch directory inside your assigned worktree and remove it before handback. The native sandbox may deny writes outside that tree. If an essential committed artifact needs another path, raise a seam request before writing it. Generated ignored build outputs are permitted only under your isolated worktree. Do not edit docs/docs-index.js directly; derive through docs-graph.py after frontmatter is complete.\n\nGround from AGENTS.md, docs/ai-forward-pack/codex.md, .agents/skills/define-architecture/SKILL.md and design-slice/SKILL.md with their stage refs, normative docs/specs/cfd-workbench-v1.md and docs/specs/foildsl.md, docs/mockups/workbench-v7.md limits, docs/notes/thick-client-shell.md, docs/proof/native-ui-workbench.md, existing ADRs, and docs/coordination/application-build.md. The first milestone is one offline native GUI plus CLI using a shared deterministic core: Example and .foil/.cfdw.json open; parse/validate→accepted lossless source→owned geometry→viewport/section inspection; one numeric independent LE or TE rail draft→preview/apply/cancel→source and semantic revision→undo/redo→atomic save/reopen with recovery draft; CLI prints the same identity/diagnostics. Analysis is honestly Unavailable. Preserve Windows/macOS intent.\n\nArchitecture decisions must start with bounded contexts, aggregate invariants and durable grain/history. Accepted source snapshots are lossless, project records append-only and immutable; no DB or second editable geometry authority for M1. Separate exact UTF-8 source SHA-256 from semantic RFC 8785/BLAKE3 identity. Pin decimal/unit→binary64 shortest-round-trip vectors and test GUI/CLI shared values. Unknown syntax/version/features reject the entire document, never silently drop fields. For geometry, prove a conservative sufficient admitted subset using interval/analytic bounds, or report Not assessed and block Apply; sampled-only validation is not a certificate. In particular test positivity on every open knot span, x derivative support per span, repeated roots/knots, thickness maximum enclosure carried through normalization, near-bound cases and bounded termination. The proposed one-profile/open-tip/independent-rail subset is a hypothesis to test, not an imposed algorithm. Atomic persistence must cover fault injection, external conflict and draft recovery without guessing history. Trace store→model→service→projection/wire→client type→UI→compute reader (Unavailable).\n\nCompare native modular monolith, WebView plus typed IPC, and native UI plus local worker. C#/Avalonia is only a candidate. Before stack commitment, execute a real macOS ARM64 native accessibility/viewport/file-dialog smoke and packaging feasibility spike with pinned candidate sources/licenses. State Windows x64 build/test/live obligations separately; do not call them passed if no Windows runner exists. The .NET 10.0.203 SDK is observed locally, not proof that Avalonia packages are installed. Use the exact assigned native spike files for a minimal candidate; write real invocation, results and limitations into docs/proof/application-spikes.md. Execute source/identity, geometry and atomic fault oracles with the exact assigned vector script or a documented temporary command; preserve reproducible inputs and output hashes in proof. A failed spike is valid evidence and may change the stack recommendation.\n\nThe documents must define public compiling core/adapters contracts and fixture shapes, including draft target/base, accepted revision, diagnostics, semantic identity, persistence/reopen, CLI parity and UI states. Do not invent implementation APIs without a spike. Name the shortest implementation path, exact upstream/downstream owned files and gates before B/C can fan out. An unresolved contradiction becomes a typed Owner decision request, not an implicit choice. Give the Owner a recommended option and compatibility/blast-radius evidence; request a numbered ruling into docs/notes/rulings.md. The Owner independently clears Data, Test and UX vetoes; you do not clear them yourself.\n\nExit evidence: descendant commit SHA, exact owned-path diff, source and command versions, observed allowed/denied/Not assessed results, docs/check gates, source hashes/identity vectors, native UI accessibility tree or smoke result, and open Owner requests. Send Coordinator done only after exit evidence is complete; if blocked, send blocked with the exact condition and retain evidence. Re-read every gate's output, not just its exit status. The compiled contract's deadline is 50 minutes, with no post-dispatch replay. Fallback is a retained brief and explicit Coordinator/Owner re-route after reviewing the failure; do not widen permissions or scope yourself.",
      "summary": "Nine owned architecture, design, security and spike source artifacts. Native .NET10/Avalonia11.3.14 candidate, accepted-source authority, conservative proof admission, exact history proposal and serial contract completion gate. Thirty oracle checks and nine certificate mismatch negatives pass; macOS native flow observed and Windows cross-build only.",
